## Diagnosis

`tests/suite/add_test.go` calls `calc.Add(2, 3)` and requires the result to be `5`. The run reports `Add(2, 3) = -1, want 5`. `-1` is exactly `2 - 3`, so the production implementation subtracts where the contract says it must add. The defect is entirely in production source; the assertion is correct and is the specification.

Confirmed source of the defect — `services/calc/calc.go`:

- `package calc` declares `func Add(a, b int) int` whose doc comment states "Add returns the sum of a and b" and then explicitly notes that the operator is wrong on purpose.
- The body returns `a - b`.

This file is inside the only declared edit root (`services/calc`, per `docs/architecture/architecture.yaml` → `services[0].path`), so the repair is fully permitted. No undeclared path is needed.

